<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebraOps</PackageId>
    <Description>Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebraOps — geometric transforms as a parametric op algebra over Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebra: a state of named objects, generic in the name, whose comparison and spelling the caller supplies; seven ops — Add an object from its parameters (a point; two points; a point and a direction; a centre, a radius and a normal; a normal and a distance; a centre and a radius), Remove, Rotate about an axis through a point, Translate, Scale about a centre, Reflect in a plane, and Screw, the general rigid motion — each carrying parameters and never a coefficient; a total apply and canApply that refuse by name and leave the state as it was; an inverse for six of the seven; the compaction of a run of rigid transforms of one object into one op; a canonical wire codec that writes every float as its IEEE-754 bit pattern; and a Fuaran.Core.OpStream StreamWitness, so a history of transforms is an append-only, hash-chained, replayable stream. Replay builds every object and every versor through the algebra's published constructors and applies it by their published sandwich, and computes nothing of its own: the same bits on .NET, under Fable and in every host that transcribes it. Fable-clean.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The ops, the state, apply, the inverse, the compaction, the codec and the stream witness,
         each written once over an internal record of its rules (Phase 731, DECISIONS.md D85 item 9,
         D90). -->
    <Compile Include="GeometricOps.fs" />
    <!-- Every public operation's exactness class, as data. -->
    <Compile Include="GeometricAlgebraOpsOperations.fs" />
    <!-- The law family over the operations above. LAST: it reads all of them. -->
    <Compile Include="GeometricAlgebraOpsLaws.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The algebra, whose published constructors and sandwich replay calls; the op-stream, whose
         witness this package supplies; the wire, whose canonical writer and reader the codec uses
         (DECISIONS.md D85 item 9). This is the only geometric package that references the op-stream. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebra\Fuaran.Compute.GeometricAlgebra.fsproj" />
    <PackageReference Include="Fuaran.Core.Wire" />
    <PackageReference Include="Fuaran.Core.OpStream" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Core" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The suite runs the shipped functions with one rule changed to show a law vector fail. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Fuaran.Core.Compute.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
